# 低频词汇 List09
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2026恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List09核心词汇

peer /pɪə(r)/ n. 同龄人 Peer pressure can influence teenage behavior. 同伴压力可以影响青少年行为。
penal /ˈpiːnl/ adj. 刑事的 The penal code was revised to include new offenses. 刑法典被修订以包括新的罪行。
pending /ˈpendɪŋ/ adj./prep. 待定的 The approval is still pending. 批准仍在等待中。
peril /ˈperɪl/ n. 危险 The sailors faced grave perils at sea. 水手们在海上面临严重危险。
permeate /ˈpɜːmieɪt/ v. 渗透 Corruption has permeated all levels of government. 腐败渗透到了政府的各个层面。
persecute /ˈpɜːsɪkjuːt/ v. 迫害 Religious minorities have been persecuted for centuries. 宗教少数派几个世纪以来一直受到迫害。
pervasive /pəˈveɪsɪv/ adj. 普遍的 Technology has become pervasive in modern life. 科技在现代生活中已经变得无处不在。
petition /pəˈtɪʃn/ n. 请愿 The petition gathered over a million signatures. 请愿书收集了一百多万个签名。
plague /pleɪɡ/ n./v. 瘟疫；困扰 The region has been plagued by drought. 该地区一直受干旱困扰。
plunge /plʌndʒ/ v./n. 骤降 Stock prices plunged after the announcement. 公布后股价骤降。
precedent /ˈpresɪdənt/ n. 先例 The ruling set an important legal precedent. 该裁决树立了一个重要的法律先例。
predecessor /ˈpriːdəsesə(r)/ n. 前任 The new CEO outperformed her predecessor. 新CEO的表现超过了她的前任。
premature /ˈpremətʃə(r)/ adj. 过早的 It would be premature to draw conclusions. 现在下结论为时过早。
premise /ˈpremɪs/ n. 前提 The argument is based on a false premise. 该论点基于一个错误的前提。
prerequisite /priːˈrekwɪzɪt/ n. 先决条件 A degree is a prerequisite for the position. 学位是该职位的先决条件。
prestige /preˈstiːʒ/ n. 威望 The award carries great prestige in the field. 该奖项在该领域具有很高的声望。
pristine /ˈprɪstiːn/ adj. 原始的 The beach was in pristine condition. 海滩处于原始状态。
profound /prəˈfaʊnd/ adj. 深刻的 Technology has had a profound impact on society. 科技对社会产生了深刻的影响。
prohibitive /prəˈhɪbɪtɪv/ adj. 禁止性的；高昂的 The cost of the treatment is prohibitive. 治疗费用高得令人望而却步。
prop /prɒp/ v./n. 支撑 The government propped up the failing bank. 政府支撑了陷入困境的银行。
prosecute /ˈprɒsɪkjuːt/ v. 起诉 The government will prosecute tax evaders. 政府将起诉逃税者。
prototype /ˈprəʊtətaɪp/ n. 原型 The engineers built a prototype of the device. 工程师们建造了该设备的原型。
proximity /prɒkˈsɪməti/ n. 接近 The school's proximity to the park is an advantage. 学校靠近公园是一个优势。
prudent /ˈpruːdnt/ adj. 审慎的 It is prudent to save for the future. 为未来储蓄是审慎的。
purge /pɜːdʒ/ v./n. 清除 The government purged political opponents. 政府清除了政治对手。
quota /ˈkwəʊtə/ n. 配额 The company introduced a sales quota system. 公司引入了销售配额制度。
rampant /ˈræmpənt/ adj. 猖獗的 Corruption is rampant in the region. 该地区腐败猖獗。
rationale /ˌræʃəˈnɑːl/ n. 理由 The rationale for the decision was clearly explained. 决定的理由得到了清楚的解释。
rebuke /rɪˈbjuːk/ v./n. 谴责 The manager rebuked the employee for negligence. 经理因疏忽谴责了员工。
reckon /ˈrekən/ v. 认为；计算 It is reckoned that over a million people attended. 据估计有超过一百万人参加。
